WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:08.290
Speaker 1: Republican Congressman Adam Kinzinger
is lashing out at Republican Congresswoman

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:09.290
Lauren Boebert.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.290
Remember that?

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:18.520
Lauren Boebert recently said, I'm sick and
tired of this separation of church and state.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.380
It's kind of the Constitution.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.610
Lauren But you're tired of it.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:27.640
Adam Kinzinger are calling it the Christian
Taliban as a reminder.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:33.670
Here is the clip from a couple of days ago.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:42.680
Lauren Boebert going full throttle theocracy
saying church and state.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:47.050
I'm sick of it.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:54.500
Speaker 2: The reason we had so many over
reaching regulations in our nation is because

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.840
the church complied.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.129
Speaker 1: Right.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:01:01.629
Speaker 2: The church is supposed to direct
the government.

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:02.629
Why?

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:08.920
Government is not supposed to direct the church.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.740
That is not how our founding fathers intended
it.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.110
And I'm tired of the separation of church
and state junk that's not in the Constitution.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.390
It was in a stinking letter.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:20.500
And it means nothing like what they say it
does.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.590
Speaker 1: Whoa.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:32.820
Well, it turns out that that is crazy.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.630
And fellow Republican launching a civil war
salvo from within the Republican Party, Adam

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:42.400
Kinzinger says, quote, There is no difference
between this.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.400
This meaning, you know, this video of Lauren
Boebert that we just watched.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.469
There's no difference between this and the
Taliban.

00:01:50.469 --> 00:01:52.980
We must oppose the Christian Taliban.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.070
I say this as a Christian.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:59.229
Has a Republican politician straight up said
Christian Taliban before because they love

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:01.220
to talk about Sharia law.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.210
And Oh, it's bad.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.729
And it's going to be it's coming and.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:08.019
Hold on a second.

00:02:08.019 --> 00:02:12.030
The Christian version of Sharia law is what
has actually been plaguing this country for

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.220
a very long time.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:17.400
I disagree with Adam Kinzinger politically,
but I have some respect for him now.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:23.170
I know it's easier to put country over party
the way that he's doing when you're leaving.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.230
I understand that.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.290
I'm not naive.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.340
I get it.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.850
He's in a position where he doesn't care because
he's leaving.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:33.420
But it is amazing how the bar has been lowered.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:38.040
Democrats today would be thrilled to some
degree to deal with the Republicans from 15

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.040
years ago.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.380
Not that those were good people.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:45.470
We shouldn't see them as good people, but
15 years ago the Republicans were much more

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:46.940
reasonable to deal with.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:57.840
That being said, the Republicans are 15 years
ago are responsible for the Republican Party

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:03.849
today being what it is.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:14.620
And what I mean by that is they didn't condemn
the start of the rhetoric that led to Trumpism

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:15.620
today.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.379
They didn't condemn the extremism.

00:03:17.379 --> 00:03:25.629
They didn't say, well, we've got to stop this
here or here or here.

00:03:25.629 --> 00:03:30.920
They allowed it to keep going.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:45.580
So while I would much rather be dealing with
the Republicans of 15 years ago than people

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.840
like Lauren Boebert, that's for sure.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:04:05.200
We also have to understand the historical
context which I talked about with many people,

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:21.030
including Noam Chomsky on the show before,
that they are also responsible for what we

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:28.890
are seeing today.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:05:04.220
But to the extent that Adam Kinzinger is willing
to call it out, to the extent that Adam Kinzinger

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:20.370
is maybe going to change some Republicans
mind and get some Republicans to go, hey,

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:32.260
you know what, the boebert version of Republicanism
is crazy.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.080
It's not even constitutional.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:39.200
Tired of separation of church and state.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.300
It's like being tired of the First Amendment.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:51.470
Lauren Which I thought you cared about to
the extent that he might have an impact on

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.470
anybody.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:54.100
I gladly welcome Adam Kinzinger, his comments

